# What does NOT ship to the marketplace.
#
# The shipped extension is four files plus one binary: dist/extension.js,
# dist/webview.js, dist/webview.css, package.json, bin/<goos>-<goarch>/composure.
# Everything else here is how it was built, and shipping it costs every
# installer the download.
#
# `make package` appends the per-target `bin/**` rules to a generated copy of
# this file, so the binaries are governed there rather than here — see the
# `package` target. Packaging by hand with a bare `vsce package` therefore
# carries every platform's binary; that is deliberate, so that a hand-run never
# silently produces a VSIX with no core in it at all.

# The marketplace screenshots. 955KB of PNGs that every installer downloads and
# no installed extension ever reads: the README renders them from
# raw.githubusercontent.com, because a marketplace page cannot resolve a
# relative path. They are tracked here so the README has somewhere to point and
# so the pictures version with the product -- not so they ship inside it.
#
# media/icon.png is the exception and must stay: package.json's `icon` field
# names it and the marketplace reads it out of the VSIX.
media/*.png
media/*.svg
!media/icon.png

# Source. The bundles in dist/ are what runs; the TypeScript is not needed to
# run them and `**/*.ts` alone would not catch the directories.
host/**
webview/**
shared/**
*.ts
**/*.ts

# Tests and their build output.
dist-test/**
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.ts

# Source maps. ~400KB of the ~600KB dist/ tree, and useless without the
# sources above.
**/*.map

# Build tooling and its inputs.
build.mjs
run-tests.mjs
tsconfig.json
node_modules/**
package-lock.json
.vscode/**
build/**

# The screenshot harness: measuring instruments, and a 900KB fixture of captured
# core answers. It renders the shipped bundle; it is not part of it, and every
# installer was paying for it.
harness/**

# Documentation that is for contributors, not users. README.md, CHANGELOG.md
# and LICENSE.txt are picked up by vsce and must not be listed here.
TESTING.md
